comments.message:
Interesting point, It does not fail to parse it with the patchset you commented on.

libpldm rejects packages with format revision higher than the pin parameter.

```
  |       if (hdr->package_header_format_revision <
  |           PLDM_PACKAGE_HEADER_FORMAT_REVISION_FR01H) {
  |       |       return pldm_msgbuf_discard(buf, -EPROTO);
  |       }
  |       if (hdr->package_header_format_revision > pin->format.revision) {
  |       |       return pldm_msgbuf_discard(buf, -ENOTSUP);
  |       }

```

If we need this restriction or not, it depends on if the meaning of certain fields in the package changes in the future or any small details like that.

I changed the behavior to do the conservative thing (as libpldm does) and simply reject the package if the actual format revision is higher than what the user code asked for.

Also implemented the test you asked for.

thanks for your review ❤️
